#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The SSA edit harness (DESIGN 4.3, item 8): each case's edits as rebuilds
of ONE `PARTEX_SSA=1` process, each stage against plain partex (the same
binary, no `PARTEX_*` variable) run on the same sources.

    scripts/sandbox scripts/ssa-edits [--case NAME]... [--bin PATH]
        [--work DIR] [--jobs N] [--fixpoint] [--check] [--env K=V]...
        [--timeout S] [--mem-gb N] [--brief]

(`cargo xtask ssa-edits` runs it on the release binary, and `cargo xtask
check` with `--brief`.)

The cases: every incremental case of `xtask/src/e2e.rs` built `By::Watch`
(read from `INCREMENTAL` there), `machine_edits` (`edits.tex`, pdflatex
format, e2e's six edits, a seventh whose glyphs the fonts have, so that
each font's union is as it was and the job's end does not run, then
letters no page had, and their removal: the end runs for each) and
`machine_edits_dvi` (`edits-dvi.tex`, latex format), both under
`-output-directory=out` after two plain runs of the original text, as
e2e's `machine_edits` seeds them; `label`: the same document given a
`\\label` nothing refers to, then rebuilt twice with no edit;
`aux_reopen` (`reopen.tex`, pdflatex format): an edit in the first
paragraph, whose step opens the `.aux` and whose page opens the PDF, its
revert, and a later edit; `garbled`: the same, the SSA side's written files
(`.aux`, `.toc`, `.out`) cut to their first line, their times kept,
before each rebuild, which must read the build's own values of them; `streams` (`streams.tex`): a line written to
the file a stream opened first, changed and back, after the stream opened
a second; `fatal_end` (`fatal-end.tex`): a word edited and back in a job
that ends fatally in its last page's output routine, not seeded: the
.aux the first build wrote is read by its next trip (or, one trip a
build, by the next stage's), which runs earlier steps again; and
`inputs` (`inputs.tex`): a file only tested for (`\\openin` and
`\\ifeof`), edited, and a line appended after the last line of a file
`\\input` (the primitive), then taken away, then a word of it changed,
the file's MD5 sum printed.

Each case runs in WORK/<case>/:
- `o/`: the oracle, one run per stage, the stage's edit made before it
  (`--fixpoint`: each stage run again while a file it wrote, but its log,
  DVI and PDF, changed, at most 5 runs, e2e's `fixpoint`);
- `p/`: one SSA process whose `PARTEX_SSA_REBUILD` lines each snapshot
  what the build before wrote, then make the next edit;
- an edit is made as e2e's `edit_file` makes it: the text with its
  marker replaced, its modification time fixed (`\\pdffilemoddate` must
  agree: inputs at 1758800000, edit k at 1758800000 + 1000 k), renamed
  over the file; an empty marker is a rebuild with no edit;
- `snap/{o,p}/<stage>/`: every file of the run directory after each stage
  (the format aside), compared stage by stage: byte for byte, and `.log`
  and `.blg` files without their first line (banner, date) and with
  `xtask/src/mask.rs`'s statistics masked, as e2e compares them;
- `streams/<stage>/`: each stream the SSA process's stores hold after
  the stage's link (`PARTEX_SSA_STREAMS`), what a load of it is served:
  it must be the file the link wrote (`include_keys`: `include`'s edits,
  each rebuild one trip, linked, then the idle settle, as an editor's);
- `logs/`: each process's terminal output and stderr; `results.json` in
  WORK holds every number.

The formats are built once per binary, in WORK/formats. Exits 1 if a stage
of a case differs or its SSA process failed, 2 on a usage error.
"""

